  "term": "abnormal psychology",
  "definition": "Abnormal psychology is the branch of psychology concerned with mental processes and experiences that differ from what is considered usual or normal. In a broad sense, it covers unusual mental phenomena as well as disturbances, impairments, and forms of mental disorder.",
